  "Question": "If a number eight times as large as \\(x\\) is increased by two, then one fourth of the result equals",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2x+\\frac12\\)",
    "B": "\\(x+\\frac12\\)",
    "C": "\\(2x+2\\)",
    "D": "\\(2x+4\\)",
    "E": "\\(2x+16\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Eight times \\(x\\) is \\(8x\\). Increasing that number by two gives \\(8x+2\\). One fourth applies to this entire result, so the requested expression is\n\\[\\frac14(8x+2)=\\frac{8x}{4}+\\frac24=2x+\\frac12.\\]\nThis is choice A.",
